Time Complexity: Time required to solve problem

1. o(1) => if operraions are constant no loop
2. o(n) => if the operations are based on inputs given EX: loop executes n time
3. o(n^2) => if the operations are exponantional and multiple of n Ex : 2 loops, 1 withinn another
4. O(log n) => divide and conquar, if array of 8 and in case of divide and conquare worst case takes 3 iteration so long2 base 3 s 8



* Best case denoted by Omega
* Average case denoted by theta
* worst case denoted by Big O
Here in DSA we only discuss worst case i.e. Big O

Rules of Big O
1. Drop constant:
if loop iterated n time but there are 2 loops one after anoter so 2n then we denote it to O(n) and drop 2 constant

2. Drop non dominant
if n^2 + n then it just o(n^2)


Note: if function takes 2 different constant and then 2 loops are thir based on those constant then can't say o(n)
because n is differnt here, we can say then O(a) + O(b)

